{"type":"text","timestamp":1794306168687,"sessionID":"ses_e3b0e6f2affe5tG5fb8cRNiCNJ","part":{"id":"prt_1c4fb0794001SZU5FEA7SwU4ZI","sessionID":"ses_e3b0e6f2affe5tG5fb8cRNiCNJ","messageID":"msg_1c4faabe50017prCN0rH40hzwL","type":"text","text":"All 4 tests pass. Here's a summary of the refactor:\n\n**Created `clients/retry.py`** — a shared `call_with_retry` function that:\n- Calls `fn()` and returns its result on success\n- Retries only `TransientError` (any other exception propagates immediately with no sleep)\n- Uses exponential backoff (`base_delay` × 2^attempt), never sleeping after the final attempt\n- Re-raises the last `TransientError` when all attempts are exhausted\n\n**Refactored `clients/orders.py`** — removed the duplicated retry loop (with `for`/`while`), now delegates to `call_with_retry` for both `get_order` and `cancel_order`.\n\n**Refactored `clients/users.py`** — fixed the bugs in the original retry logic:\n- It was catching all `Exception` instead of just `TransientError` (permanent errors were being retried)\n- It used a fixed 0.1s delay instead of exponential backoff (should be 0.1 → 0.2)\n- It was always sleeping even after the last attempt\n- Now delegates to `call_with_retry`, which handles all of this correctly.","time":{"start":1794306148244,"end":1794306168687}}}
